    {
      "@id": "https://www.gov.uk/id/service/change-driving-test",
      "@type": "GovernmentService",
      "name": "Change your driving test appointment",
      "description": "Find an earlier practical driving test, move it to a later date, or change the test centre you take it at.\r\n",
      "url": "https://www.gov.uk/change-driving-test",
      "identifier": [
        {
          "@type": "PropertyValue",
          "propertyID": "local:govuk-path",
          "value": "/change-driving-test"
        }
      ],
      "provider": {
        "@id": "https://www.gov.uk/id/organization/d39237a5-678b-4bb5-a372-eb2cb036933d",
        "name": "Driver and Vehicle Standards Agency"
      },
      "areaServed": {
        "@id": "https://www.gov.uk/id/jurisdiction/gb",
        "name": "United Kingdom"
      },
      "serviceStatus": "active",
      "lifeEvent": [
        "vehicle"
      ],
      "keywords": [
        "Driving, motorcycle and LGV instructor qualification process",
        "Car driving tests",
        "Driving tests and learning to drive or ride",
        "Teaching people to drive"
      ],
      "availableLanguage": [
        "en-GB"
      ],
      "dateModified": "2026-09-02",
      "availableChannel": [
        {
          "@type": "ServiceChannel",
          "serviceUrl": "https://driverpracticaltest.dvsa.gov.uk/login",
          "name": "Continues on the driving test booking service"
        }
      ],
      "applicationProcess": "You can change your driving test appointment: 2 times if you’re changing a car driving test 6 times if you’re changing any other type of test What you can change When you change your appointment, you can: find an earlier driving test (sometimes called a ‘cancellation appointment’) move your driving test to a later date change which test centre you take your test at You can change more than one thing at the same time. Example If you change your test from Northampton on 4 June to Kettering on 12 May, this counts as one change. You can change your test up to the time your test starts. You must give notice to change or cancel a test, or you’ll have to pay again. When you’ll have to pay again You’ll have to pay again if you give less than: 10 full working days’ notice for car driving tests 3 full working days’ notice for all other tests Monday to Saturday count as working days but Sundays and public holidays do not. If you cannot change your driving test appointment, cancel your test . What"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://www.gov.uk/id/service/check-eta",
      "@type": "GovernmentService",
      "name": "Check your electronic travel authorisation (ETA)",
      "description": "Check when your electronic travel authorisation (ETA) expires and what to do if you’ve changed your passport or need a new ETA to visit the UK.",
