          "serviceUrl": "https://view-immigration-status.service.gov.uk/view/checker-details"
        }
      ],
      "applicationProcess": "Use this service to check someone’s immigration status if you have their ‘share code’. The share code will have been emailed to you or given to you by the person whose status you’re checking. It expires after 90 days. You will also need the person’s date of birth. The service will show if they have the right to live in the UK, and any restrictions on their rights or access to benefits and services. Use a different service to check someone’s right to work or to check their right to rent ."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://www.gov.uk/id/service/make-a-sorn",
      "@type": "GovernmentService",
      "name": "Register your vehicle as off the road (SORN)",
      "description": "Register your vehicle as off the road - you will not need to pay vehicle tax until you put it on the road again",
      "url": "https://www.gov.uk/make-a-sorn",
      "identifier": [
        {
          "@type": "PropertyValue",
          "propertyID": "local:govuk-path",
          "value": "/make-a-sorn"
        }
      ],
      "provider": {
        "@id": "https://www.gov.uk/id/organization/70580624-93b5-4aed-823b-76042486c769",
        "name": "Driver and Vehicle Licensing Agency"
      },
      "areaServed": {
        "@id": "https://www.gov.uk/id/jurisdiction/gb",
        "name": "United Kingdom"
      },
      "serviceStatus": "active",
      "lifeEvent": [
        "vehicle",
        "tax"
      ],
      "keywords": [
        "Buying, selling, registering and scrapping a vehicle",
        "Buy, sell or scrap a vehicle",
        "Build or adapt a vehicle",
        "Number plates, vehicle registration and log books",
        "Vehicle tax, MOT and insurance"
      ],
      "availableLanguage": [
        "en-GB"
      ],
      "dateModified": "2026-09-02",
      "availableChannel": [
        {
          "@type": "ServiceChannel",
          "serviceUrl": "https://www.sorn.service.gov.uk"
        }
      ],
      "applicationProcess": "Tell DVLA you’re taking your vehicle off the road, for example if you’re keeping it in a garage. This is sometimes called a ‘Statutory Off Road Notification’ ( SORN ). This page is also available in Welsh (Cymraeg) . You’ll get a refund for any full months of remaining tax. You cannot use the vehicle on the road until you tax it again . You do not need to make a SORN for a vehicle you’ve already sold. Tell DVLA you’ve sold a vehicle instead. Apply to take your vehicle off the road Your SORN will start immediately if either: your vehicle tax has expired you’re not applying in the month your vehicle tax is due to expire Your SORN will start on the first day of the next month if you apply in the month your vehicle tax is due to expire. Apply online You can apply online if the vehicle is registered in your name. Start when you’re ready to take your vehicle off the road. You can apply using the: 11-digit number in your vehicle log book (V5C) 16-digit reference number on your vehicle tax rem"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://www.gov.uk/id/service/sign-in-to-manage-your-student-loan-balance",
      "@type": "GovernmentService",
      "name": "Manage your student loan balance",
      "description": "Sign in to your student loan repayment account - check your balance, make regular or one-off repayments, or let SLC know if your details have changed. ",
